course: dictionary
lesson: 11547
title: Amharic, a language of Ethiopia
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amharic is a noun when it names a language, just as English and French do. «Our class learned to write our names in Amharic.» The word Amharic tells you which language the class learned.
explain: Amharic can also be an adjective, a describing word that means about that language. «The Amharic letters looked like tiny shapes.» Here Amharic describes the letters: they belong to that language.
explain: When you meet a word you do not know, look at the words around it. In «She studied Amharic at school», the word school and the word studied are clues that Amharic is a subject, so it is a language. Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Amharic is the main working language of Ethiopia, a country in East Africa.
fact: Amharic is written in its own script, called Ge'ez or Fidel.
fact: Fidel is an alphabet of syllables, where each symbol stands for a consonant and a vowel together.
fact: Amharic is a Semitic language, related to Arabic and Hebrew.
fact: «Amharic» can be a noun, meaning the language, or an adjective, meaning about that language, as in «an Amharic textbook».
exercise: What is Amharic? | *A language of Ethiopia | A kind of dance | A type of bread | A country in Africa
exercise: «The Amharic letters looked like tiny shapes.» What does Amharic describe here? | *The letters, which belong to that language | The sea and the sky | The children in the class | The shapes, which are round
exercise: Which language is Amharic related to? | *Arabic and Hebrew | Chinese and Japanese | Welsh and Irish | French and Spanish
test: «Amharic is written in Fidel, an alphabet of syllables.» What is Fidel? | A bus | A river | *The script that Amharic is written in | A kind of food
test: Ella says Amharic is a noun in this sentence: «She studied Amharic at school.» Is she right? | *Yes, it names a language | No, it is a verb that means to study | No, it is a place | No, it describes a person
exam: Which statement about Amharic is true? | Amharic is a country in Asia | Amharic is a type of music | Amharic is written in Roman letters only | *Amharic is the main working language of Ethiopia
